 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You need water. So you dig a hole until it fills up from the ground. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the walls are just loose dirt, and one night they cave in.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you line the hole with concrete rings. Now it stays open!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But pulling up one bucket at a time takes forever.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you cap the well and add a hand pump. Push the handle, and water comes out!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But in a dry summer, the water drops deeper. And a pump on top can only pull water up about twenty five feet.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you lower an electric pump all the way down. It pushes the water up instead, straight to a tank.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Gravel around the bottom keeps the sand out, and a sealed cap keeps dirty rain out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a water well. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
